---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="GC Fitness — Privacy Policy">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-container">
      <p class="legal-lang"><a href="/gc-fitness/privacy">Versión en español</a></p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy — GC Fitness</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Effective date: September 27, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy describes how Golden Crow ("we") handles your personal data when you use the
        <strong>GC Fitness</strong> mobile app (package <code>com.goldencrow.fitness</code>,
        available for iOS and Android). GC Fitness is a coaching platform: it connects each client
        with their personal trainer.
      </p>

      <h2>Data we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account:</strong> name, email address, and profile photo provided by your
          sign-in method (Google or Apple).</li>
        <li><strong>Training and health data:</strong> logged workouts (sets, reps, weights,
          durations), habits and their completion, body metrics you enter (weight, height),
          personal records, and goals.</li>
        <li><strong>Progress photos:</strong> photos you voluntarily upload for visual
          tracking.</li>
        <li><strong>Messages:</strong> your chat with your coach (text, photos, and voice notes)
          and, if you use the social features, direct messages with other people (text
          only).</li>
        <li><strong>Social features (optional):</strong> your public profile (@handle, name, photo,
          and bio), who you follow and who follows you, follow requests, who you've blocked, the
          routines you publish, your comments, likes and saved routines, and the reports you send.
          See <a href="#social">Social features</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchases:</strong> the history of your in-app subscriptions and purchases (not
          your card details, which the store handles).</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> device push token (FCM), crash reports (Firebase
          Crashlytics), and product-usage events (Firebase Analytics: e.g. "workout started",
          "set logged", screen views — associated with your user ID). We do not use advertising
          identifiers.</li>
        <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> language, theme, units, notification settings, and
          timezone.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Providing the service: your trainer sees your workouts, habits, metrics, progress
          photos, and messages in order to coach you.</li>
        <li>App functionality: syncing across your devices, notifications (workout and habit
          reminders, coach messages, rest-timer alerts).</li>
        <li>Diagnostics and improvement: crash reports and product analytics.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        On iOS, with your permission, the app writes your workouts to Apple Health and reads data
        such as heart rate, active energy, and steps to display them in the app. Apple Health data
        is processed on your device and is never used for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Health Connect (Android)</h2>
      <p>
        On Android, GC Fitness can connect to <strong>Health Connect</strong> to complete two
        features. This is optional: the rest of the app works without it, and you can withdraw
        access at any time from within Health Connect (or from Settings → Health → Health Connect
        inside GC Fitness, which takes you there).
      </p>
      <p>We request <strong>read access to exactly two record types</strong>, and no others:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Steps</strong> — your daily step totals. We use them to draw the Steps chart on
          your Progress tab, and we store the daily total in your own record in our database so
          that <em>your coach</em> can see how active you are between training sessions.</li>
        <li><strong>Heart rate</strong> — the samples recorded during a workout you complete in the
          app, read only for that workout's time window. We use them to draw the heart-rate line
          on that workout's summary (with its minimum, average and maximum) and we store that
          series alongside that workout, visible to you and to your coach.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Read-only.</strong> GC Fitness never writes data to Health Connect, and never reads
        any health data other than the two record types above.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Sharing.</strong> Data read from Health Connect is shared only with the coach
        assigned to you — the purpose of the service — and with Google Firebase as our
        infrastructure processor (see below). It is <strong>never used for advertising, never sold,
        and never shared with any other third party</strong>. We do not transfer it to any
        advertising or analytics network.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Retention and deletion.</strong> Step totals and workout heart-rate series are kept
        with the rest of your training data while your account is active, and are deleted with it
        when you delete your account (Settings → Delete account). Withdrawing the Health Connect
        permission stops any further reading immediately; to also remove what was already stored,
        delete your account or write to us at
        <a href="mailto:support@goldencrowvs.com">support@goldencrowvs.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="social">Social features</h2>
      <p>
        The social features are optional. This is what other people see when you use them:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your public profile</strong> (@handle, name, photo, bio, and follower and
          following counts) can be seen by anyone with a GC Fitness account. If your profile is
          <strong>private</strong>, your routines and follower lists are only visible to people you
          have accepted. The photo is the same as your account photo.</li>
        <li><strong>The routines you publish</strong>, with their comments and likes, can be seen by
          anyone with an account who has access to your profile, and by anyone who has the
          routine's link on the web. Your logged workouts, habits, metrics, and progress photos are
          <strong>never</strong> published.</li>
        <li><strong>Direct messages</strong> can only be sent between people who follow each other,
          and only the two participants can see them.</li>
        <li><strong>Blocks</strong> are only visible to the person who blocks: the blocked person is
          not notified.</li>
        <li><strong>Searches</strong> for people are not stored: we only count how many you make per
          day to limit abuse.</li>
        <li><strong>Suggestions:</strong> we suggest public routines based on the routines you
          have and who you follow.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Moderation.</strong> When someone reports content (a profile, a routine, a comment,
        or a message), our moderation team can see that content and its context to decide whether
        it breaches the <a href="/en/gc-fitness/terms">Terms of Use</a>. The reported person never
        learns who reported them.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your trainer:</strong> sees the fitness data, photos, and messages associated
          with your account — that is the purpose of the service.</li>
        <li><strong>Other people who use GC Fitness:</strong> only what you publish through the
          social features, as described above.</li>
        <li><strong>RevenueCat:</strong> processes the status of your subscriptions and purchases to
          unlock Premium. It acts as a data processor.</li>
        <li><strong>Infrastructure providers:</strong> we use Google Firebase (authentication,
          database, storage, push notifications, Crashlytics, and Analytics) to operate the app.
          Google acts as a data processor.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>We do not sell your data.</strong> There are no ads, and we never share your data
        with third parties for marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>Security and storage</h2>
      <p>
        Your data is stored on Google Cloud (Firebase) and encrypted in transit (TLS). Access is
        restricted by security rules: only you and your trainer can access your data, except what
        you publish through the social features.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your data while your account is active. You can delete your account at any time
        from the app (Settings → Delete account) or by emailing us — see
        <a href="/en/gc-fitness/delete-account">Account deletion</a>. Deletion removes your
        profile, workouts, habits, metrics, photos, and messages; a minimal anonymized record
        (no name or email) is kept for system integrity, and crash/analytics telemetry is removed
        per Firebase's retention windows.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you used the social features, deleting your account also deletes your public profile,
        who you followed and who followed you, your requests and blocks, the routines you
        published, your likes and saved routines, and your direct messages. From your comments we
        remove the text, name, and photo; an empty placeholder remains so other people's replies
        don't break. Your @handle stays reserved for 90 days so nobody can impersonate you. We keep
        the reports you <em>sent</em> about other people's content, and the copies other people
        already made of your routines, which are theirs.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can request access to, correction of, or deletion of your data by writing to
        <a href="mailto:support@goldencrowvs.com">support@goldencrowvs.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The app is not directed at children under 13.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy we will publish the updated version on this page with a new
        effective date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Golden Crow — <a href="mailto:support@goldencrowvs.com">support@goldencrowvs.com</a>
      </p>

      <p>
        See also the GC Fitness <a href="/en/gc-fitness/terms">Terms of Use</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: 7rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    min-height: 60vh;
  }
  .legal-container {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .legal-container h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .legal-container h2 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-container ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .legal-container li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .legal-updated {
    opacity: 0.7;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .legal-lang {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
</style>
